    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This podcast examines why soccer, the world's most popular sport, is barely the fourth most popular sport in the United States. It explores why Americans looked down upon the game in the 1800's as well as why its popularity did not see significant growth throughout the 1900's. The podcast features interviews with renowned professors of American history as well as immigration and ends with a brief speculation on whether soccer's popularity will take off in the 2000's.",
